# Copy to .env and fill in.  .env is gitignored — never commit it.
#
# One key to get. The LLM needs none.
#
# ============================================================
# Baidu index via SerpApi — REQUIRED
# ============================================================
# Email signup, no card, 250 free searches/month.
#   https://serpapi.com/users/sign_up  ->  https://serpapi.com/manage-api-key
#
# Not optional. Baidu results are injected into the prompts so stage 0 resolves
# an English company name against real Chinese search results rather than
# guessing — and stage 0's output is the Chinese registry name that the filings
# and patent channels search on. No key, no 宇树科技, no filings. The run stops
# at startup rather than completing with an almost-empty corpus.
#
# Baidu retired its official search API, so this is a vendor running the query
# and parsing Baidu's result page, not a first-party API.

SERPAPI_KEY=

# Several keys rotate when one exhausts its monthly quota. Numbered variables
# are read in order and reading STOPS at the first gap, so _2 must exist before
# _3 is seen. The free tier is per account; check SerpApi's terms before
# stacking accounts to get past it.
# SERPAPI_KEY_2=
# SERPAPI_KEY_3=


# ============================================================
# LLM: Claude Code CLI — no key
# ============================================================
# The CLI carries its own authentication, so there is nothing to put here.
#   curl -fsSL https://claude.ai/install.sh | bash
#   claude          # sign in once
#   claude --version
#
# It shares your interactive Claude Code usage allowance, so a long run can
# slow your own session down.
#
# Optional overrides:
# CLAUDE_CLI_BINARY=claude
# CLAUDE_CLI_MODEL=
